inline-c (dependency: stdlib/logic.tur miniKanren engine). The fixture body is
pure-turi and exercises compiled HKT instance resolution for Goal, but it loads
logic.tur, whose ~22 inline-C primitives implement a full miniKanren: tagged
term constructors/accessors (term-int/var/pair/nil + term-tag/-int-val/-var-id),
unification, the substitution store, walk, reify-walk, and run-logic threading
state through the Backtrack stream. Re-implementing that whole engine as
interpreter natives is disproportionate for a single fixture and is library
internals, not a language-level gap -- carve per the R3 fix-vs-carve rule in
docs/archive/history/turi-interpret-flip-residual-plan.md. (The companion
hkt-stdlib-backtrack-instances IS fixed: backtrack.tur's cons-stream monad
reduces to a handful of natives, registered in wk_register_backtrack_natives.)
